    "description": "Metrus Energy finances, owns, and manages energy efficiency, renewable energy, and resiliency upgrades for commercial, industrial, higher education, and other institutional customers. Its customers use the company's energy-as-a-service structure to procure building and onsite energy infrastructure without upfront capital spending, while projects are installed and maintained through partner contractors. The business follows an asset-heavy, contracted model in which project cash flows are tied to long-term service agreements rather than merchant energy sales. Public disclosures state that Metrus has operational projects in 32 states across more than 760 sites, giving it a broad national footprint in distributed decarbonization infrastructure. ECP acquired the company in July 2022, and Metrus has since continued to scale its platform around energy efficiency, distributed generation, cooling, heating, and related low-carbon infrastructure.",
